! BRANCH RELATIVE is not implemented, and says so.
!
! HOW THIS WAS FOUND.  audit_opcode_coverage-style screening of the
! assembler's mnemonic tables against every program turned up 23
! mnemonics STRAP can emit that no program uses.  Most are documented
! scope limits -- EX, EXIC, RNX, LOC, the radix-conversion family.  BR
! was not: bsv/README.md listed it among the IMPLEMENTED unconditional
! branches, "B BR BE BD BEW NOP", and the model branched on it exactly
! as it branches on B.
!
! TWO PRIMARY SOURCES SAY THAT IS WRONG.
!
!   X22-6533 pocket card, UNCONDITIONAL BRANCHING: B is 010000000 and
!   BR is 011000000, a DIFFERENT operation code, and BR is named
!   "Branch Relative".
!
!   Reference Manual p.42: "A simple storage of the instruction counter
!   without branching action is accomplished by STORE INSTRUCTION
!   COUNTER IF BRANCH RELATIVE with a branch address of 0."  A branch
!   address of 0 producing NO BRANCHING ACTION is only possible if the
!   address is a displacement.  Under the old absolute reading it would
!   have branched to 0.0 -- which p.39 also calls an invalid branching
!   address ("the addresses between 0.0 and 31.32 are invalid branching
!   addresses"), so the old behaviour was wrong twice over.
!
! WHY NOT JUST IMPLEMENT IT.  The base is almost certainly the stepped
! instruction counter -- p.39: "after an instruction is fetched, but
! before its execution, the instruction counter contents are stepped in
! ordinary fashion... prior to any attempt to replace the instruction
! counter contents" -- so the counter already holds the fall-through
! during execution, and fall-through + 0 is exactly "no branching
! action".  But whether the displacement is SIGNED, and in what UNITS,
! is not established by anything read so far.  Implementing it would be
! a guess dressed as a fix.  Failing loud is the honest state, and it
! replaces a SILENT WRONG BRANCH with a visible unimplemented operation.
!
! WHAT THIS PROGRAM PINS: that BR sets OP and does not branch.  It uses
! the OP indicator pinned by op_ad_indicators.strap.  When someone
! implements Branch Relative, this program is what fails, and the
! comment above is what they need.

        SLC, (8)2500.0
START   BB, $OP, $                   ! hang up if OP on -- must start off
        BR, FAIL                     ! not implemented: sets OP, no branch
        BZB, $OP, $                  ! hang up if OP off
        B, PASS                      ! BR must have fallen through to here
FAIL    BEW, $                       ! BR branched: wrong, and the deck
                                     !   would have gone somewhere absolute
PASS    BEW, $
        END, START
